  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with real entries,   there is a corresponding negative matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice if $A\\in S$ then \n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot |A|=|A|\\ne 0,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in S.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any matrices $A,B\\in S,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nA+(B-C)=A+(B+(-C))=(A+B)+(-C)=(A+B)-C\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
